{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal multiprofile setup using scvi_n200 RNA encoder, imagenet_vit_l image encoder (replacing resnet50), avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion. Validation accuracy of 0.7150 and F1 of 0.6872 suggest the more complex image encoder may improve performance compared to previous multimodal baselines (e.g., 0.6315 accuracy in llm_summary_008). However, the RNA-only scvi_n200 model (0.6501 accuracy) still outperforms this configuration, leaving uncertainty about the relative contribution of image encoder complexity versus RNA encoding and the potential interactions with aggregation/fusion strategies."
}

